@tradition postcard-night
// Postcard night (0.60.7): write a card home (the writing hobby's tradition) at the booth row; it goes out with the
// next mail run. Eklund keeps the cards and the box (the deck architect's postcard box).
k: 446
title: Postcard night
when: weekly thursday
at: 18:45-19:45
min: 20
where: 3 room Call-home booths: bench
where: 3 room Promenade: bench
hold: 1
who: eklund-leila always, calls-home 45%, quiet-corner 25%, everyone 10%
anim: read
host: eklund-leila
from: eklund-leila
invite: host=eklund-leila odds=30% line="Postcard night, by the booths. I've got spare cards. Write one home?"

== mail
- Postcard night tomorrow, {time}, by the call-home booths. Cards and pens on me. They go out with the next mail run.

== ask
- Postcard night later. I never know what to write. I write it anyway.   #warm
- Eklund's got new cards. One's got the Wren on it.
- Write one home tonight? Your family would like a card.   #warm

== here
- How do you spell "nebula"? Asking for my mum.   #funny
- Short is fine. They just want to know you're well.   #warm
- Leave room for a drawing. Everyone does a drawing.

== thanks
- You write a card home by the booths and drop it in Eklund's box. It goes out with the next mail run.   #warm

== chatter
- My gran keeps every card I send on her fridge. It's a big fridge.   #funny
- Postcard night's quiet. Just pens, and people thinking about home.   #warm
